      "content": "I hear the intensity of that guilt, but this judgment seems to stem from holding an ideal of heroism rather than human reality. When someone is in mindless panic, they may choose default comfort instinctively before fear kicks in, meaning that stillness doesn't necessarily mean malice or a choice to harm someone. It is often more compassionate to view yourself as someone currently in heavy pain rather than someone who is fundamentally irredeemable.",
